abstract: >
  We present Symbiose, a cognitive architecture that combines
  graph-based causal reasoning, temporal pattern recognition,
  and proactive autonomy to enable persistent, evolving
  collaboration between humans and AI. Components are integrated
  through Quantum Leap (QL), a persistent cognitive orchestration
  layer. Every response is tagged via an L0–L3 epistemic framework
  distinguishing canonical facts (L0) from derived inferences (L1),
  document-supported claims (L2), and LLM-generated hypotheses (L3).
  Through deployment in cosmological theory development (Energy-Flow
  Cosmology), we demonstrate emergent capabilities not achievable
  in stateless architectures: cross-session identity linking,
  hierarchical memory consolidation, proactive suggestion generation,
  and explicit provenance tracking.
